\chapter{Global Simulation Architecture}

\section{Overview}

The Global Simulation Architecture defines the unified computational framework
that governs all dynamical processes within the MPS--PCE system. It integrates
heterogeneous biological modules, numerical solvers, uncertainty quantification,
and closed-loop countermeasure optimization into a single coherent execution
graph.

The architecture is designed to support:
\begin{itemize}
    \item multiscale biological modeling,
    \item stochastic and deterministic dynamics,
    \item high-throughput Monte Carlo replication,
    \item distributed execution across cloud and edge nodes,
    \item cryptographically verified computation.
\end{itemize}

\section{Global State Definition}

At any simulation time $t$, the global state vector is defined as:
\[
\mathbf{G}(t)
=
\big(
\mathbf{S}_{A}(t),\,
\mathbf{S}_{B}(t),\,
\mathbf{S}_{C}(t),\,
\mathbf{S}_{D}(t),\,
\mathbf{S}_{\text{infra}}(t),\,
\mathbf{S}_{\text{sec}}(t)
\big),
\]
where:
\begin{itemize}
    \item $\mathbf{S}_{A}(t)$: genetic dysregulation state,
    \item $\mathbf{S}_{B}(t)$: pathogen kinetics state,
    \item $\mathbf{S}_{C}(t)$: trauma physiology state,
    \item $\mathbf{S}_{D}(t)$: cellular senescence state,
    \item $\mathbf{S}_{\text{infra}}(t)$: infrastructure health/load,
    \item $\mathbf{S}_{\text{sec}}(t)$: cryptographic verification state.
\end{itemize}

\section{Execution Operator}

The simulation evolves according to the global execution operator:
\[
\mathbf{G}(t_{k+1})
=
\mathcal{E}
\Big(
\mathbf{G}(t_k),\,
\mathbf{\Omega}(t_k),\,
\mathbf{U}(t_k)
\Big),
\]
where:
\begin{itemize}
    \item $\mathbf{\Omega}(t_k)$ is the diagnostic observation vector,
    \item $\mathbf{U}(t_k)$ is the countermeasure vector,
    \item $\mathcal{E}$ is the unified evolution operator.
\end{itemize}

