\section{Diagnostic Ingestion Layer}

The diagnostic ingestion layer transforms raw clinical measurements into
normalized state vectors:
\[
\mathbf{\Omega}(t)
=
\mathcal{I}
\big(
\mathbf{X}_{\text{CBC}},
\mathbf{X}_{\text{CMP}},
\mathbf{X}_{\text{NAAT}},
\mathbf{X}_{\text{NGS}}
\big),
\]
where $\mathcal{I}$ is the ingestion operator.

Normalization:
\[
\tilde{x}_i = \frac{x_i - \mu_i}{\sigma_i}.
\]

\section{Parameter Mapping}

Each module receives a parameter set:
\[
\Theta
=
\{\Theta_A,\, \Theta_B,\, \Theta_C,\, \Theta_D\},
\]
computed via:
\[
\Theta_i = \mathcal{T}_i(\mathbf{\Omega}(t)).
\]

\section{Unified Dynamics}

The global dynamics are defined by:
\[
\frac{d\mathbf{G}}{dt}
=
\mathcal{F}
\big(
\mathbf{G}(t),\,
\Theta,\,
\mathbf{U}(t)
\big),
\]
where $\mathcal{F}$ is the unified dynamical operator.

\subsection{Coupling Terms}

Coupling between modules is expressed as:
\[
\mathbf{C}_{ij}(t)
=
\Gamma_{ij}
\big(
\mathbf{S}_i(t),\,
\mathbf{S}_j(t)
\big),
\]
with $\Gamma_{ij}$ representing cross-module influence.

\section{Closed-Loop Countermeasure System}

Countermeasures are computed via:
\[
\mathbf{U}(t)
=
\mathcal{C}
\big(
\mathbf{G}(t),\,
\Theta
\big),
\]
where $\mathcal{C}$ is the control operator.

Policy convergence:
\[
\left\|
\mathbf{U}^{(k+1)}(t)
-
\mathbf{U}^{(k)}(t)
\right\|
\le
\epsilon_{\text{policy}}.
\]

\section{Distributed Execution Model}

The simulation is distributed across nodes:
\[
\mathcal{N}
=
\{\text{Edge}_i,\ \text{Regional}_j,\ \text{Core}_k\}.
\]

Bandwidth:
\[
B_{ij}
=
\frac{S}{\tau_{ij}},
\]
where $S$ is packet size and $\tau_{ij}$ is latency.

\section{Security Binding}

All simulation steps are cryptographically verified:
\[
\text{Verify}_{\text{ZKP}}
\big(
\mathbf{G}(t),\,
\mathbf{U}(t)
\big)
=
\text{true}.
\]

Audit hash:
\[
H(t)
=
\text{SHA3}
\big(
\mathbf{G}(t)
\parallel
\mathbf{U}(t)
\parallel
t
\big).
\]

\section{Global Error Metrics}

Global NMAE:
\[
\text{NMAE}_{\text{global}}
=
\frac{1}{N}
\sum_{i=1}^{N}
\frac{
\left|
\hat{\mathbf{\Omega}}_i(t)
-
\mathbf{\Omega}_{\text{true},i}(t)
\right|
}{
\bar{\mathbf{\Omega}}_{\text{true},i}
}.
\]

\section{Summary}

The Global Simulation Architecture provides the structural backbone of the
MPS--PCE system, enabling multiscale modeling, distributed computation,
cryptographic verification, and closed-loop optimization. It ensures that all
biological, computational, and infrastructural components operate as a unified,
coherent simulation engine.